WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:05.220
Viserys Targaryen: For three hundred years
the Targaryen dynasty stayed strong, in the

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.740
face of rebellion, civil war, and plague.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.650
But the line of dragon kings was broken when
my father, Aerys Targaryen, the Second of

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.980
His Name, was overthrown in rebellion.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.860
My father was betrayed and slaughtered by
Ser Jaime Lannister, a member of his own Kingsguard.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.300
His son and heir, my brother Rhaegar, perished
on the field of battle at the hands of Robert

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.390
Baratheon, who claimed the Iron Throne for
himself.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.800
Robert Baratheon: "Ours is the Fury."

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.000
These are the words of the black stag of Baratheon.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.370
A battle cry echoed throughout the land in
rebellion, when I, Robert Baratheon, the First

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:55.690
of His Name, seized the Iron Throne from the
Mad King, Aerys Targaryen, ending a dynasty

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.040
nearly three hundred years old.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.650
After Aegon's conquest of the Seven Kingdoms,
the Baratheons remained loyal enough to the

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:07.550
crown while Targaryen kings came and went.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.840
But loyalty has its limits.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:18.360
When Rhaegar Targaryen, Aerys' vile son and
heir, abducted Lyanna Stark, my betrothed,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.950
my beloved, it was time to act.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.790
We raised our banners.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:31.030
Baratheon, Stark, Jon Arryn, and the Tullys,
united in rebellion against Rhaegar and his

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.950
father, the Mad King.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.250
We were victorious and took the Iron Throne.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:43.659
That bit of dragon blood in my veins came
in well as it made me a distant relation to

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:49.290
the Targaryen dynasty blood of my long-lost
ancestor, Orys.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.840
The truth of it is I took it.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.740
Brynden Tully: Under the Targaryens, the Riverlands
knew a peace we hadn't had for centuries,

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.210
if ever.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:04.869
But like all good things, sooner or later,
it all goes to shit.

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:08.399
And our shit had a name.

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:10.929
Aerys Targaryen.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:15.540
Westeros has had its share of Mad Kings, but
usually, they had the sense not to bully more

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.390
than one powerful house at a time.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.639
Aerys soon blundered into a triple alliance.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:25.650
The North, Stormlands, and Vale rose against
him.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.549
But of course, where do you think most of
the blood was spilled?

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:33.730
My brother Hoster guaranteed the answer to
that with the marriage of my niece to Eddard

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.680
Stark, the Warden of the North.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.010
At least Hoster didn't send her to Robert.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:45.250
So, the Riverlands joined the war against
the Mad King; and it was on one of our rivers

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:50.909
that Prince Rhaegar died, sealing the fate
of his dynasty.

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:54.790
Robert was a great soldier and a horrible
king.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:03:01.169
Catelyn Stark: Whatever the case, House Frey
does nothing so well as survive.

00:03:01.169 --> 00:03:06.639
When the ironborn conquered and razed the
Riverlands, the Freys hid in their castle.

00:03:06.639 --> 00:03:13.010
When Aegon and House Tully swept the ironborn
back to their islands, the Freys hid in their

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.010
castle.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:19.519
When my ancestor demanded their allegiance
as Aegon's new Lord Paramount of the Trident,

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:24.249
the Freys bent the knee from their castle.

00:03:24.249 --> 00:03:28.969
Perhaps then we should not have been surprised
when my father, Lord Hoster Tully, called

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:33.919
his banners against the Mad King and Lord
Walder didn't answer.

00:03:33.919 --> 00:03:40.359
The Baratheons, Starks, Arryns, and Tullys,
some of the oldest and greatest houses of

00:03:40.359 --> 00:03:46.799
Westeros, fought and bled for the cause of
justice while House Frey hid in its castle

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:48.760
and waited.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:53.629
No doubt if Rhaegar had won at the Trident,
Lord Walder would have given him safe passage

00:03:53.629 --> 00:04:00.689
into the North to destroy the rest of my husband's
Northern army for a fair price.

00:04:00.689 --> 00:04:07.219
But Rhaegar fell and, lo and behold, the Frey
army appeared to render aid to our already

00:04:07.219 --> 00:04:09.590
victorious forces.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:15.150
Many sniggered that Lord Walder had been waiting
for his army to come of age, having fielded

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.110
it out of his own breeches.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:23.139
My own father named him The Late Lord Frey
to the other lords' amusement.

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:26.300
In many ways, however, Lord Walder was wise.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:32.370
We had no guarantee of victory and had he
fought with us from the outset and we failed,

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:36.110
he would have lost the bridge his family was
so proud of.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:39.180
"More Pride Than Honor."

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.790
those should be the words of House Frey.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:47.710
Yet part of me wonders if Lord Walder waited
not out of fear but hope.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:53.930
That we would be destroyed, leaving him to
assume my family's place as Lord Paramount

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.740
of the Trident.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.629
To buy the respect they have always wanted,
but refused to earn.

00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:05.750
Brienne of Tarth: Targaryen rule quieted the
Stormlands for the most part until Robert

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.900
rebelled against the Mad King.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:13.050
His first challenge came not from the Crown,
but from his own bannermen who tried to join

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.539
forces against him.

00:05:15.539 --> 00:05:20.490
Robert struck first, defeating three armies
in a single day at Summerhall.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:24.789
The victory cemented Robert's control of the
Stormlands, and he was able to march on the

00:05:24.789 --> 00:05:28.819
Reach and Riverlands with no enemy to his
rear.

00:05:28.819 --> 00:05:32.410
Yet not all of Robert's bannermen sided with
him.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:38.530
Ser Barristan the Bold came from the Stormlands,
but as the preeminent member of Aerys's kingsguard

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:42.780
and greatest knight in the realm, Ser Barristan
remained loyal.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.620
After Robert's decisive victory on the Trident,
Robert sent his own maester to care for his

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:51.960
countryman Ser Barristan, who had suffered
grievous wounds while fighting so hard to

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.400
kill him.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:59.960
Later, when the Kingslayer betrayed Aerys,
Robert pardoned Ser Barristan and even took

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.020
him onto his own kingsguard.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:07.789
Catelyn Stark: House Arryn remained loyal
to the Targaryen dynasty.

00:06:07.789 --> 00:06:16.729
Until Lord Jon Arryn joined with Houses Baratheon
and Stark in rebellion against Mad King Aerys.

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:23.530
Upon winning the Iron Throne, Robert named
Lord Jon Hand of the King, a position he held

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.930
until his mysterious death.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:31.659
Littlefinger: The Vale's isolation does breed
an abundance of honor and pious bleating,

00:06:31.659 --> 00:06:35.050
which governs their decisions instead of foresight.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:40.090
Like a blind man who can only guess where
his horse is taking him, I doubt Jon Arryn

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:44.819
had even prepared for civil war when he raised
his banners instead of handing over his young

00:06:44.819 --> 00:06:48.370
wards, Ned Stark and Robert Baratheon, to
the Mad King.

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:51.529
Honor demanded, and Lord Arryn obeyed.

00:06:51.529 --> 00:06:56.819
He'd have done the same if the boys hadn't
been the lords of two great houses, who could

00:06:56.819 --> 00:06:59.249
field mighty armies of their own.

00:06:59.249 --> 00:07:01.569
But perhaps I give him too little credit.

00:07:01.569 --> 00:07:08.700
After all, if the war went against them, only
Lord Arryn had a nice impregnable castle to

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:14.319
retreat into; and he was wise enough to take
poor Lysa Tully into his bed to win the Riverlands

00:07:14.319 --> 00:07:15.939
as allies.

00:07:15.939 --> 00:07:19.050
Jon Arryn won, then Jon Arryn died.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:22.909
Margaery Tyrell: The Reach stayed loyal.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.099
Mostly.

00:07:24.099 --> 00:07:30.289
My father, Mace, dealt Robert his only defeat
in the war, even if it was my father's vanguard

00:07:30.289 --> 00:07:33.129
who did most of the fighting before he arrived.

00:07:33.129 --> 00:07:38.360
After the Battle of Ashford, we laid siege
to Storm's End, Robert's home.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:44.180
Unfortunately, the war ended before we could
take it and free up our armies to go save

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.650
the king.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:50.550
Some may question my father for laying siege
to the Baratheon's home instead of marching

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:55.539
to aid Prince Rhaegar before Robert could
kill him and scatter the royal army.

00:07:55.539 --> 00:08:01.770
But let us not forget that we had already
dealt Robert his only defeat of the war at

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:02.770
Ashford.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:09.610
If Lord Tywin Lannister had not "vanquished"
the Mad King so suddenly, our siege would've

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:14.529
destroyed Robert's home and his brothers and
won the war for Aerys.

00:08:14.529 --> 00:08:21.389
But when the Targaryens fell, House Tyrell
again chose peace and prosperity over war

00:08:21.389 --> 00:08:26.840
and devastation, and bent the knee to King
Robert Baratheon, First of His Name.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:30.970
Jaime Lannister: I remember the day the Lord
Commander wrote my name down in the White

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.630
Book, the official record of the Kingsguard.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:39.010
At sixteen, the youngest member ever to join,
knighted by Ser Arthur and Ser Barristan for

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.560
valor against the Kingswood Brotherhood.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:45.360
An outlaw had decided to try his luck against
a lowly squire.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:49.500
He was not using his head, so I took it off
him.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:53.910
Shortly afterwards, King Aerys the Second,
who hadn't yet earned the title of the Mad

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.420
King, took me into his service.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.519
If I have ever been happy, it was that day.

00:09:00.519 --> 00:09:04.449
Everyone in his kingdoms soon knew the names
and sang the songs of the Kingsguard.

00:09:04.449 --> 00:09:07.730
I certainly did from earliest days.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:13.620
Lord Commander Gerold Hightower, the White
Bull; Arthur Dayne, the Sword of the Morning.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.800
Bronn: Arthur Dayne, Gerold Hightower.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:21.480
Sure, if half the stories about them are true,
they could swing a sword better than most.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.959
Makes their lives even more of a waste.

00:09:23.959 --> 00:09:27.990
Bodyguards to the maddest king the Seven Kingdoms
ever saw.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.620
Watching their king burn men alive.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:35.160
Hiding the Stark girl that Prince Rhaegar
stole away, causing a war that toppled their

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.540
king.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:40.050
And all this without any gold or women to
show for it.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.930
Stupid buggers!

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:44.860
The only one with any sense was Jaime Lannister.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:48.850
When his father stormed the city, he put a
sword through the Mad King's back rather than

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.680
die gloriously at his post.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:52.680
He's still here.

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:53.950
They are not.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:56.370
Oberyn Martell: My sister, Elia.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:10:02.209
She married Prince Rhaegar Targaryen and became
the Princess she already was.

00:10:02.209 --> 00:10:05.880
In Dorne, she walked among vipers, and none
would bite her.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:10.820
In King's Landing, she found herself surrounded
by lions.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:15.329
When Robert Baratheon rebelled against his
rightful king, his future father-in-law, Tywin

00:10:15.329 --> 00:10:22.899
Lannister, ordered his beast Gregor Clegane
to murder my sister along with her helpless

00:10:22.899 --> 00:10:23.899
children.

00:10:23.899 --> 00:10:26.880
And men call the Lannisters "heroes."

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.750
Hallyne: Dragons conquered the Seven Kingdoms.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:36.720
But to rule them, the Targaryens needed a
less temperamental tool.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:43.110
When the great King Maegor saw the power of
the Alchemists' Guild, he blessed us with

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:44.779
his patronage.

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:52.320
In those days, we commonly transmuted metals
and other wonders, but the King was most interested

00:10:52.320 --> 00:11:00.370
in our mastery of the Substance, which those
not of our order dub "wild-fire."

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:07.190
After the unfortunate Prince Aerion Targaryen,
drunk with wine, boasted that a draft of the

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:14.199
Substance would transmute him into a dragon,
we lost our royal favor.

00:11:14.199 --> 00:11:19.279
Then came the wise King Aerys, Second of His
Name.

00:11:19.279 --> 00:11:25.790
I was merely an acolyte when he restored our
Guild to its former glory.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:32.970
As had his great forefathers, he appreciated
our secret arts, even naming Wisdom Rossart

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:35.019
as Hand of the King.

00:11:35.019 --> 00:11:41.889
Together, they punished his enemies as befits
a true Targaryen.

00:11:41.889 --> 00:11:50.600
During the War of the Usurper, I heard whispers
that King Aerys had engaged our greatest Wisdoms

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.649
for an ultimate weapon against his foe.

00:11:53.649 --> 00:12:01.209
But, sadly, King's Landing must have fallen
before it could be used, and many of our Wisdoms

00:12:01.209 --> 00:12:04.839
disappeared in the sack of the city.

00:12:04.839 --> 00:12:10.650
Victims of ignorance and envy as ever, I'd
wager.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:15.949
Littlefinger: The realm had no sharper minds
than Lord Tywin Lannister, Hand to King Aerys

00:12:15.949 --> 00:12:21.060
Targaryen, or as history remembers him, "The
Mad King."

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:27.250
He saw assassins and plots in every shadow,
heard whispers in silence, and burned men

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:32.399
alive, but his greatest madness by far was
driving away Lord Tywin.

00:12:32.399 --> 00:12:36.990
The Mad King then cycled through every mistake
of his ancestors.

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:42.600
Soldiers, toadying lords and at the end, even
an alchemist, perhaps to save the crown's

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:44.490
growing expenses on wildfire.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.689
Unfortunately, it didn't save his crown or
his dynasty.

